        "original_id": "b2d3a5b5-15ca-5075-a4e5-cd654913da3d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: American Scientist, Dwell\n- Organizations: Sigma Xi, The Scientific Research Society\n- People: Lara Hedberg Deam, Karrie Jacobs\n- Topics: science and technology magazines, design publishing\n\nFacts:\n- American Scientist is an American bimonthly science and technology magazine that has been published since 1913.\n- Sigma Xi, The Scientific Research Society, has published American Scientist since 1913.\n- American Scientist is informally abbreviated as AmSci.\n- In September 2000, Dwell was launched as a magazine to bridge the gap between design professionals and enthusiasts.\n- Lara Hedberg Deam launched Dwell.\n- Karrie Jacobs served as Dwell's Editor-in-Chief at its launch.",
